english_question:
Given the following conditions: 
1. ∠1 = ∠2; 
2. ∠3 = ∠4; 
3. AD ∥ BE, and ∠D = ∠B; 
4. AD ∥ BE, and ∠DCB = ∠BAD; 
Which of the following conditions can lead to AB ∥ DC? 
A. 1, 2 
B. 2, 4 
C. 2, 3 
D. 2, 3, 4

In quadrilateral \(ABCD\), it is known that \(AB=BC=CD\), and both angles \(∠BAD\) and \(∠CDA\) are acute. Point \(F\) is a point on diagonal \(BD\), line \(EF\) is parallel to \(AB\) and intersects \(AD\) at point \(E\), line \(FG\) is parallel to \(BC\) and intersects \(DC\) at point \(G\). Quadrilateral \(EFGP\) is a parallelogram, and the following conclusions are given: 
\(①\) Quadrilateral \(EFGP\) is a rhombus; 
\(②\triangle PED\) is an isosceles triangle; 
\(③\) If \(∠ABD=90^{\circ}\), then \(\triangle EFP\) is congruent to \(\triangle GPD\); 
\(④\) If quadrilateral \(FPDG\) is also a parallelogram, then \(BC\) is parallel to \(AD\) and \(∠CDA=60^{\circ}\). 
The correct conclusion numbers are ______ (fill in all correct conclusion numbers on the line).
